      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  Can this function call crec_flash_response_fill_banks() instead and then just print out information from the struct ec_response_flash_info_2 response?\n\nThe problem with this approach is that we don\u0027t know how many banks we have. `struct ec_response_flash_info_2` doesn\u0027t allocate memory for banks. It would get complicated quickly.\n```\nstruct ec_response_flash_info_2 {\n\t/* Total flash in the EC. */\n\tuint32_t flash_size;\n\t/* Flags; see EC_FLASH_INFO_* */\n\tuint32_t flags;\n\t/* Maximum size to use to send data to write to the EC. */\n\tuint32_t write_ideal_size;\n\t/* Number of banks present in the EC. */\n\tuint16_t num_banks_total;\n\t/* Number of banks described in banks array. */\n\tuint16_t num_banks_desc;\n\tstruct ec_flash_bank banks[0];\n} __ec_align4;\n```\n\nInstead, I added `flash_get_region()` function which provides information about the region, of which the sector is a part. Function returns true if there are more regions, false otherwise.\n\nSurprisingly, it started to look easier to me 😊",
